  "notes": {
    "semetey-2-2013:p0005:b003:l014": "Dangyt is retained as an ethnonym; the dative construction is rendered as dividing the slain among them, though the precise violent idiom is uncertain.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0005:b003:l034": "Томук is rendered literally as an ankle bone in the torture sequence; the exact punitive practice is uncertain.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0005:b005:l006": "The obscene dismissal of the dream as fox dung and Bozbala as Karagul's dung is preserved directly.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0005:b005:l016": "Oen is retained as a personal name or patronymic referent; its identity is uncertain.",
    "semetey-2-2013:p0005:b005:l024": "Бакшы is retained as bakshy, a shamanic diviner or healer, in the clairvoyant-dream context."
  },
